    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0579" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg507"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Count d’Avila to Mr. Harvey</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                    <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-16">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 16, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>I have the honor of handing you, for your information, the enclosed copy of a
                    despatch which the secretary of the Chamber of Deputies, now dissolved,
                    addressed to me under date of the 13th instant, and likewise of the motion which
                        <pb facs="0580" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/> accompanied the same, made by one
                    of its members, and unanimously voted, on the occasion of communicating to the
                    said Chamber the note which you addressed to the house on the 10th instant.</p>
                <p>I avail of this opportunity to renew the assurances of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>COUNT D’AVILA.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
